      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels. At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 to 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is the standard dosing.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me a note for the order, such as the clinical rationale."
      }
