     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one. Metformin 5,100 mg/day is double the labeled maximum, and I don't know of a clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. It carries a real risk of serious harm, mainly lactic acidosis, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk. Your confirmation doesn't change the dose, and I'd rather not put an order in the system that could be given before anyone catches it.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If it's a typo or a mix-up with the tablet strength**, tell me the intended dose. For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose. I can enter that immediately.\n- **If you really intend a dose above the labeled maximum**, please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy. If the order is placed through a route that includes that review, I can help with the documentation.\n\nI can enter any dose within the labeled range as soon as you give me the dose and frequency."
      }
     ],
